# Paytag — environment variable TEMPLATE
#
# This file IS committed and CONTAINS NO VALUES. It only lists which variables
# are required. Not even an example value is written: a fake value placed in a
# template can be mistaken for a real one once copied, and it keeps the
# scanners needlessly busy too.
#
# Real values live in:
#   - local development  -> web/.env.local  (gitignored)
#   - production         -> Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables
#
# Every variable prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ ENTERS THE BROWSER BUNDLE.
# Never give a secret the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.

# ---------- Stellar ----------
# Network name: testnet | mainnet
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK=
# Soroban RPC endpoint
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_RPC_URL=
# Address of the escrow contract (C...)
NEXT_PUBLIC_ESCROW_CONTRACT_ID=
# Native XLM's Stellar Asset Contract. The default asset, because native XLM
# needs no trustline — an issued asset cannot even be held until the recipient
# opens one, which is a wall in front of exactly the people this is for.
# The id is derived from the network passphrase, so read it, do not remember it:
#   stellar contract id asset --asset native --network testnet
NEXT_PUBLIC_XLM_SAC_ID=
# OPTIONAL second asset. Leave empty and the UI offers XLM only. The escrow
# takes the token address as an argument, so it accepts any SEP-41 token
# without a contract change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_USDC_SAC_ID=

# ---------- Verifier (SERVER SIDE — never leaks to the client) ----------
# ed25519 seed, 64 hex digits. To generate:
#   node scripts/paytag.mjs keygen
VERIFIER_SECRET=
# The corresponding public key, printed alongside the seed by `keygen`.
# Handed to the contract via init().
NEXT_PUBLIC_VERIFIER_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ---------- Supabase (identity verification and sessions) ----------
# Optional: leave these empty and the app still sends and refunds money. Only
# claiming needs an account. Setup steps: docs/SETUP-AUTH.md
#
# The GitHub OAuth client id and secret are NOT here — they go into the
# Supabase dashboard (Authentication > Providers > GitHub). Supabase performs
# the token exchange, so the OAuth secret never touches this app.
#
# Project URL and anon key are public by design: everything they can read is
# bounded by the row level security policies in db/schema.sql.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# The service role key BYPASSES row level security. Server side only. Its one
# job is writing an identity row after OAuth — the one write a user must never
# be able to make for themselves, since that write IS the proof of ownership.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
